\DOC GHOST_INTRO_TAC

\TYPE {GHOST_INTRO_TAC : term -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Rewrites the precondition of an {ensures} goal, replacing every occurrence of a
state-dependent component expression by a fresh variable and appending a
conjunct equating the component to that variable.

\DESCRIBE
The first argument {t : term} is the variable (of the component's value type)
that stands for the component's value in the precondition; the second argument
{comp : term} is the component reader, given either as a partially applied read
function or as a lambda over the state producing the value, whose occurrences
in the precondition are abstracted. All subterms of the form "{comp} applied to
the state" in the precondition (the first state predicate) are replaced by {t},
and a conjunct stating that {comp} of the state equals {t} is appended at the
end of the precondition's conjunction; the precondition's conjuncts are also
re-associated to the right, so any bracketing in the original is flattened. The
substitution reaches inside nested binders and quantified subformulas of the
precondition. The postcondition and the frame are left as they are, and
occurrences of the component there are untouched.
{
      A ?- ensures ...
      ==========================================  GHOST_INTRO_TAC t comp
      A ?- ensures ...   (precondition rewritten as above)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the tactic performs exactly this single transformation
of an {ensures} goal, always producing exactly one subgoal.

\ENDDOC
